463	 * A blocked process can only be resumed in user mode, so waitpid cannot
464	 * simply continue where it left off.  Instead the caller is blocked on the
465	 * child's wait list and `sepc` is rewound onto the `ecall`, so once the child
466	 * exits the system call is executed again -- this time finding the child
467	 * gone (or a zombie ready to be reaped).  The return value has to be `pid`
468	 * in that case because handle_syscall() writes it back into a0, which is the
